/Contents (World History \055 Module 2\072 WWII and the Post\055War Order\012\0124\056 WWII Outbreak and Global Scale\072\012World War II \0501939\2051945\051 broke out on September 1\054 1939\054 when Nazi Germany invaded Poland\054 leading Great Britain and France to declare war\056 The conflict pitted the Axis Powers \050Germany\054 Japan\054 Italy\051 against the Allied Powers \050Great Britain\054 the Soviet Union\054 the United States\054 and China\051\056 Key turning points included the Battle of Stalingrad on the Eastern Front\054 the Pacific Battle of Midway\054 and the June 6\054 1944 \050D\055Day\051 Allied invasion of Normandy\056\012\0125\056 Atomic Era and United Nations\072\012WWII concluded in Europe in May 1945 following the fall of Berlin\054 and in Asia in August 1945 after the United States dropped atomic bombs on Hiroshima and Nagasaki\056 The post\055war order established the United Nations \050UN\051 in October 1945 to foster international security and diplomatic resolution\056 Tensions between the United States and the Soviet Union soon initiated the Cold War\054 a decades\055long rivalry characterized by nuclear arms expansion and global proxy conflicts\056)
/DS (font\072 normal normal 9pt Helvetica\073text\055align\072left\073color\072\043000000)
